3. Serializable interface
The Serializable interface belongs to the java.io package.


Important points:

Serializable is a marker interface.

It does not contain methods that the class must implement.

It tells the JVM that objects of the class are eligible for default serialization.

A class must implement Serializable (or inherit it from a serializable superclass) for ordinary Java object serialization.

If an object contains a non-transient field referring to a non-serializable object, serialization can fail with NotSerializableException.


The transient keyword tells Java to exclude that field from default serialization.
म्हणजे एखादा variable Serialization करताना Save करायचा नसेल तर transient वापरतो.

When deserializing, a transient instance field receives its default value unless it is explicitly restored through custom deserialization logic.


