Q6) What is Shallow Copy?

Shallow Copy creates a new object but copies the references of nested objects. Therefore, both objects share the same nested objects. Changes to shared nested objects affect both objects.

***********

class Address {
    String city;

    Address(String city) {
        this.city = city;
    }
}

class Student {
    int id;
    Address address;          // Nested object reference

    Student(int id, Address address) {
        this.id = id;
        this.address = address;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Address a1 = new Address("Pune");

        Student s1 = new Student(101, a1);

        // Shallow Copy
        Student s2 = new Student(s1.id, s1.address);

        s2.address.city = "Mumbai";

        System.out.println(s1.address.city);
        System.out.println(s2.address.city);
    }
}

***************Output:
Mumbai
Mumbai

