Q7) What is Deep Copy?

Deep Copy creates a new object along with new copies of its nested objects. Therefore, both objects are completely independent, and changes in one object do not affect the other.

********
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Address a1 = new Address("Pune");

        Student s1 = new Student(101, a1);

        // Deep Copy
        Student s2 = new Student(
            s1.id,
            new Address(s1.address.city)
        );

        s2.address.city = "Mumbai";

        System.out.println(s1.address.city);
        System.out.println(s2.address.city);
    }
}

***********Output:
Pune
Mumbai